hen we decide to focus on
all that is good in our
lives, happiness increases,
blood pressure drops, and heart rate
decreases [6, 7]. Unfortunately, in
orthopaedic surgery, it can be challenging to stop and take note of all of
the good stuff. There just are too many
things on the to-do list. Not enough
time in the day, it seems. Perhaps we

