precipitate is then filtered out to have potable water. The primary source of the iron in the water is geologic. Iron is
abundant in iron-bearing minerals; hence it could be derived from minerals like goethite, haematite, and limonite in the
Benin Formation or from plant debris in the alluvial soils [19].
